      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Citrus_City%2C_Texas"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Howard Moffitt, the founder of Citrus City, was a builder known for his unique vernacular cottage architectural style.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Citrus_City%2C_Texas"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A few of the original Moffitt houses still survive today within Citrus City.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Citrus_City%2C_Texas"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Plans for a large town were revised after the local irrigation system proved too saline for fruit production.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Citrus_City%2C_Texas"
    },
    {
